  {
   "id": 616706,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "President Lyndon B. Johnson authorized a dramatic escalation of U.S. military involvement in Vietnam in 1964 primarily because",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1174128,
     "content_html": "South Vietnam was on the verge of political and military collapse"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174127,
     "content_html": "the public overwhelmingly rejected the policy of containment"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174126,
     "content_html": "a close electoral victory had called for dramatic action to win more public support for the president"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174125,
     "content_html": "China and the Soviet Union had troops amassed on the border, ready to invade South Vietnam"
    }
   ],
